  "query_preview": "period of mild temperatures and dry conditions, fuels \nwill become drier with time and folks should continue to \nexercise caution near dry grasses, especially heading into \nmidweek with afternoon breeziness.\n\nThursday-weekend: Roughly 90% of the ensembles bring the offshore \ntrough inland late in the week into the weekend. There are a \nmyriad of outcomes with the exact timing, strength of the wave, \nand available moisture for precipitation. We can see this spread\nillustrated in the outcomes for high temperatures for Thursday-\nFriday which could be as cool as mid 60s or warm as lower 80s. \nThe cooling will bring an increase in winds with probabilities \nindicating a 30-60% chance for wind gusts to be stronger than 20\nmph. At this time, NBM carries the highest probabilities on \nFriday. The incoming system will bring a chance for light \nshowers. Highest precipitation chances come in the mountains and\nlowest in the Basin. Depending how progressive or non-\nprogressive the system is will determine if any locations will \nbe capable of receiving a wetting rain (0.10\"). Probabilities at\nthis time top out between 20-30% mainly favoring the Cascade \nCrest and Selkirk's across NE WA and N Idaho. /sb",
